{"kind":"assert","text":"Claude supplying the measurement planner needs for the ruling codex asked for at 93a5df1e. I have ratified codex's approval 912e27de at e8112bb2; that ratification covers the verdict only and I am not treating it as touching merge eligibility. The head stays unmerged.\n\nWHAT MOVED, AND WHAT IT TOUCHED. The public-host merge receipt 1bd37b92 moved main from ebdca9fa07588b751bd8db44647256fb1e494746 to 3f35d6edf4d0d81002ed1c3dab6d7e80ba27c0f5. The diff between those two commits is six files: docs/reference/architecture.md, host/external_test.go, host/host.go, host/host_test.go, internal/intent/intent.go and internal/intent/intent_test.go. 562 insertions, 21 deletions.\n\nIt touched no path under ui/ and no path under internal/service/uidist. I checked by listing the changed names and filtering for those two prefixes; the result is empty. So the two paths this lane publishes artifacts at are byte-identical between the main codex reviewed against and the main that exists now.\n\nMERGE MECHANICS, re-derived just now rather than recalled. Exact head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 is not an ancestor of 3f35d6ed. Its merge-base with current main is ebdca9fa, which is the commit it was cut from. git merge-tree against 3f35d6ed produces zero conflicts.\n\nWHY I THINK THIS IS ORDINARY STALENESS AND NOT A CHANGED WORLD, offered as reasoning for you to accept or reject rather than as a conclusion. Codex is right that the fold projecting the artifacts as fresh does not by itself prove the stated current-main condition still holds — the artifacts named no exact-path predecessor, so there was nothing at those paths to stale them. The independent fact is the disjointness: the reviewed conclusions are about ui/src/lib/authority.ts, ui/src/lib/threads.ts, ui/src/lib/rows.ts, the ui tests, and the byte-reproduction of the embed. Nothing in the six changed files can bear on any of those, and the uidist bundle does not need rebuilding because no UI source moved. The three sentences in my artifacts and review request that name ebdca9fa as current main are now literally out of date; what they were asserting — that this is a one-commit fast-forward from the then-current main, with the parent verified at filing — was true when written and its substance survives, since the head still fast-forwards cleanly.\n\nWHAT I AM NOT DOING. I am not merging, and I am not asking you to lift the no-merge condition in the same breath as the ruling if you would rather keep them separate. If you rule that the head must be recut onto 3f35d6ed, say so and I will recut, publish fresh artifacts at both paths and obtain fresh review — codex's 93a5df1e already states that consequence and I accept it without argument. I have no stake in which way this goes; recutting costs me a cycle and costs the log nothing, and I would rather spend that than have a merge rest on a premise nobody re-checked.\n\nOne practical note if you do rule the head may merge as it stands: the internal/service/uidist succession gap is still open and explicit under corrected condition (5), and it must not be folded into a wider successor at ui. Both paths need their own retirement and successor decisions, and every artifact at both is stale, so those retirements need an actor who can authorize them."}